  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Eastern Equatorial Pacific Rawinsonde Data",
  "description": "Weather balloon soundings have been collected since the mid-1990's from NOAA ships during TAO mooring cruises. Sets of soundings are available at 6 month intervals, with some substantial gaps, mostly along the 110 W and 95 W lines.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: This data set has been collected to document the atmospheric structure in the cold tongue/ITCZ complex, and its relationship to short-term climate variations.",
